{
    "title": "Board Evaluation: Process and Performance Assessment",
    "summary": "The page outlines the annual Board Evaluation process, emphasizing its role in good corporate governance, transparency, and accountability. It details the evaluation scope, covering the Board, Committees, and individual Directors, including the Chairman, and lists mandatory Committees. The process, led by the Nomination and Remuneration Committee, uses questionnaires based on SEBI guidelines, managed confidentially via a Board application by an independent agency. It describes feedback consolidation, reporting to NRC and Board, and review meetings. The evaluation criteria include Director contributions, meeting effectiveness, Board composition, strategy, governance, risk, ethics, and management performance. Independent Directors assess Non-Independent Directors, the Board, and information flow. The page also covers the Board's overall performance evaluation parameters and actions taken on prior year feedback.",
}
